                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "35922874-d239-32f3-bc64-7f7a95724e96",
                        "entry_id": "7b88be0d-5e9b-3497-b4e1-09aa4cf41044",
                        "glosses": [
                            "als krankhaft empfundenes/rücksichtsloses Streben nach Besitz/Geld oder dessen Vermehrung"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c5889f78-e1d7-4150-b544-a20afed89cce",
                                "sense_id": "35922874-d239-32f3-bc64-7f7a95724e96",
                                "text": "„Somit, meine Herren, ist der Nachweis unwiderleglich geführt; Betrügerei, niedrige Gewinnsucht, freche Unredlichkeit bis zum empörenden Frevel – das sind die Züge, die den Angeklagten charakterisieren.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ded391f2-b8bf-4803-8821-9fb9405dc13f",
                                "sense_id": "35922874-d239-32f3-bc64-7f7a95724e96",
                                "text": "„Aber eben diese rasende Gewinnsucht führte mich zum Abgrunde – ich wurde ein Spieler, und verlor oft an einem Abende wieder, was ich in vielen andern Tagen gewonnen hatte.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "96f5212a-63e4-4234-a8fb-7156ac183317",
                        "source_entry_id": "7b88be0d-5e9b-3497-b4e1-09aa4cf41044",
                        "source_sense_id": "35922874-d239-32f3-bc64-7f7a95724e96",
                        "source_sense_description": "als krankhaft empfundenes/rücksichtsloses Streben nach Besitz/Geld oder dessen Vermehrung",
                        "target_lang_word": "acquisitiveness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "acquisitiveness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8a08bd12-04f6-312a-9562-72c4a26a9eb0",
                                        "entry_id": "8de08d7e-fd9d-3f4e-b895-2a312e71c3e4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality of being acquisitive; propensity to acquire property; desire of possession."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df90e6a5-f942-489f-997f-e8c5825e2053",
                                                "sense_id": "8a08bd12-04f6-312a-9562-72c4a26a9eb0",
                                                "text": "Collecting at its best is very far from mere acquisitiveness; it may become one of the most humanistic of occupations, seeking to illustrate, by the assembling of significant reliques, the march of the human spirit in its quest of beauty, and the aspirations that were [its] guide."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ca911a1-493a-4bba-b13e-3dc006d74c8f",
                                                "sense_id": "8a08bd12-04f6-312a-9562-72c4a26a9eb0",
                                                "text": "If we win this war and have the Cotton Kingdom of our dreams, we still have lost, for we will become a different people and the old quiet ways will go. The world will be at our doors clamoring for cotton and we can command our own price. Then, I fear, we will become like the Yankees, at whose money-making activities, acquisitiveness and commercialism we now sneer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "190509b3-b245-49ac-89ec-fef3dec2eff3",
                                                "sense_id": "8a08bd12-04f6-312a-9562-72c4a26a9eb0",
                                                "text": "Rud did not even attempt to fish. Chiffan caught nothing, and for the most part they paddled about the lake, pulled yellow and white water lilies out of sheer acquisitiveness, or sprawled in the punt and meditated under a great yellowing horse-chestnut that overhung the water, and occasionally plopped a conker through its glassy surface."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "54dddcd8-9845-41a3-809b-b48b7c4450f6",
                                                "sense_id": "8a08bd12-04f6-312a-9562-72c4a26a9eb0",
                                                "text": "1952, Patricia Highsmith (as Claire Morgan), The Price of Salt, New York: Norton, 2004, Chapter Eleven, p. 113,\nI think he picked me out like a rug for his living room, and he made a bad mistake. I doubt if he’s capable of loving anyone, really. What he has is a kind of acquisitiveness, which isn’t much separate from his ambition."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4bb1296d-dc70-3fe2-b4aa-c72bdf9e5f7f",
                                        "entry_id": "8de08d7e-fd9d-3f4e-b895-2a312e71c3e4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The faculty to which the phrenologists attribute the desire of acquiring and possessing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d9a961ee-39ab-41d9-9e9e-ba20cb47a47f",
                                                "sense_id": "4bb1296d-dc70-3fe2-b4aa-c72bdf9e5f7f",
                                                "text": "Had she a little more of the organ of Acquisitiveness in her head—a little more of the love of property in her nature, she would take a good-sized sheet of paper and write plainly out, in her own queer but clear and legible hand, the story that has been narrated, the song that has been sung to her, and thus possess what she was enabled to create."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bc061efe-5c39-4d8e-b46a-87f00f594956",
                        "source_entry_id": "7b88be0d-5e9b-3497-b4e1-09aa4cf41044",
                        "source_sense_id": "35922874-d239-32f3-bc64-7f7a95724e96",
                        "source_sense_description": "als krankhaft empfundenes/rücksichtsloses Streben nach Besitz/Geld oder dessen Vermehrung",
                        "target_lang_word": "lucre",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "lucre",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "348083d7-a826-3884-bdb1-471ebfc7ebff",
                                        "entry_id": "aab859ec-9c09-3844-bbbb-5d88d0421f20",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Money, riches, or wealth, especially when seen as having a corrupting effect or causing greed, or obtained in an underhanded manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c56ea26-8a45-48a2-8d32-819eaa608109",
                                                "sense_id": "348083d7-a826-3884-bdb1-471ebfc7ebff",
                                                "text": "A Biſhop then muſt be blameleſſe, the huſband of one wife, vigilant, sober, of good behauiour, giuen to hoſpitalitie, apt to teach; / Not giuen to wine, no ſtriker, not greedy of filthy lucre, but patient, not a brawler, not couetous; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0a888bf-d847-45c6-9dea-6d8fb4c8c82e",
                                                "sense_id": "348083d7-a826-3884-bdb1-471ebfc7ebff",
                                                "text": "By-ends and Silver-Demas both agree; / One calls, the other runs, that he may be / A ſharer in his lucre; ſo theſe two / Take up in this World, and no further go."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ff698ff-c67f-4d0a-ab47-03d879ab5ac0",
                                                "sense_id": "348083d7-a826-3884-bdb1-471ebfc7ebff",
                                                "text": "When a man bargains for the price of maintaining such or such principles, or of endeavouring to make out such or such a case, without believing in the soundness of the principles or the truth of the case; such a man, whether he touch the cash (or paper-money) before or after the performance of his work, and whether he work with his tongue or his pen, may, I think be fairly charged with seeking after \"base lucre;\" for he, in such case, manifestly sells not only the use of his talents, but his sincerity into the bargain, and drives a traffic as nearly allied to soul-selling as any thing in this world can be; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "02d369d1-9261-4a80-b32b-620bc9491df7",
                                                "sense_id": "348083d7-a826-3884-bdb1-471ebfc7ebff",
                                                "text": "[…] [I]t's only fair that you should pocket the lucre. I've had my share already."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
